course: dictionary
lesson: 5426
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must use the context to find the right one. The words around lag show you which meaning the writer means. «In the cold, dark, narrow passage he lags behind, gets frightened, rushes forward and knocks Rat into Mole and Mole into Badger.» Here lags behind means moves more slowly than the others and falls behind.
explain: «Kai blames lag online, but he loses offline too, on the same sofa.» The word online is your clue. Kai is playing a game, so lag means a delay on the screen, not a slow walker. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then swap your meaning in and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Lag can also be a noun, a delay between two things. Lightning and thunder happen at the same time, but light travels faster than sound, so you see the flash before you hear the thunder. That short gap is a time lag, and you can use it to work out how far away a storm is.
fact: Lag means to move or develop more slowly than others, so you fall behind.
fact: A lag, or time lag, is a delay between one thing happening and another.
fact: In online games and video calls, lag is when the screen freezes or jumps because the internet is slow. «Lag is a delay between what you press and what happens in an online game.»
fact: Jet lag is feeling tired and muddled after flying across many time zones. Flying east is often harder.
fact: To lag pipes or a hot-water tank means to wrap them in material to keep the heat in, which stops pipes freezing in winter.
exercise: «In the cold, dark passage he lags behind, gets frightened and rushes forward.» What does lags behind mean here? | Sings loudly | Jumps over a wall | *Moves more slowly and falls behind | Goes fastest of all
exercise: «Kai blames lag online, but he loses offline too.» What does lag mean in this sentence? | A type of fast car | *A delay in the game, when the screen freezes or jumps | A soft, warm blanket | A bag for sweets
exercise: Lightning comes before thunder, and there is a short lag between them. What is a lag? | A loud crash | A flash of bright light | *A delay between one thing happening and another | A kind of weather
test: Jet lag means what? | Wrapping pipes in material | *Feeling tired and muddled after flying across many time zones | A type of sweet | Being very good at football
test: Why do people lag pipes? | To make them louder | To make them shine | *To keep the heat in, so they do not freeze in winter | To paint them a new colour
exam: In the UK, an old lag is slang. What does it mean? | A teacher who sets lots of homework | *A person who has been in prison many times | A very old pipe | A person who is always late
